self.__next_f.push([1,"Field technicians often complete paperwork after leaving the equipment site. This creates extra administrative work, increases the chance of missing important details, and delays action on safety-critical problems.\nFieldMate lets technicians document inspections by speaking naturally while they work. AssemblyAI transcribes the technician’s voice in real time. FieldMate then converts each completed observation into a structured finding containing the affected equipment, severity, recommended action, and required parts.\nTechnicians can use natural voice commands to mark an issue as critical, correct a previous finding, add a replacement part, create a follow-up task, or complete the inspection. Critical findings immediately trigger a visible safety warning.\nWhen the inspection is complete, FieldMate calculates the overall status and creates a reviewable professional PDF report. Completed and in-progress inspections are stored in Supabase, providing a history of job IDs, equipment context, findings, tasks, recordings, status, and safety flags.\nThe application also supports typed observations when microphone access or real-time transcription is unavailable. A deterministic local parser provides an additional fallback if AI extraction cannot be reached.\nFieldMate helps technicians capture accurate information while details are fresh and gives maintenance teams faster access to actionable findings."])
self.__next_f.push([1,"23:T523,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"Field inspections often force technicians to choose between doing the work and documenting it. Notes get delayed, details disappear, and urgent safety issues can be buried in a report written hours later.\n\nFieldMate lets technicians document an inspection by speaking naturally while they work. AssemblyAI provides the real-time transcription layer. FieldMate processes each completed observation and converts it into a structured finding with equipment context, severity, a recommended action, and any required part. A critical observation triggers a visible safety warning, while spoken follow-up requests become task cards.\n\nAt the end of the inspection, the technician says “complete the inspection.” FieldMate derives the overall status and creates a clean PDF report. Completed and in-progress inspections are stored in Supabase, where teams can review job history, pass or action-required status, and safety flags.\n\nThe current demo is designed for a single technician and requires no sign-in. If microphone access is unavailable, typed observations use the same extraction pipeline.\n\nFieldMate reduces the gap between what a technician sees and what the organization records. It gives field teams faster documentation, clearer maintenance actions, and immediate visibility into safety-critical findings."])
self.__next_f.push([1,"24:Ta80,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"PlantAI is an agentic computer vision system designed to help farmers, agricultural students, researchers, and plant-care professionals identify plant diseases quickly and make more informed decisions.\n\nPlant disease diagnosis is often dependent on manual inspection or expert knowledge, which can be slow, subjective, and difficult to access—especially when symptoms look similar across different diseases. A wrong or uncertain diagnosis can lead to inappropriate treatment, crop loss, and unnecessary use of pesticides.\n\nPlantAI addresses this problem through an AI-powered diagnosis pipeline that combines computer vision with agentic evidence verification. Users interact with a simple interface by uploading an image of a plant leaf. The computer vision model analyzes the image and predicts the most likely disease. Instead of relying only on a single classification result, PlantAI uses an ensemble of deep learning models to improve prediction reliability.\n\nThe system combines EfficientNetV2-S, ConvNeXt-Tiny, and Swin-Tiny through weighted ensemble learning. A supervisor agent then coordinates additional evidence-gathering steps, including retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), disease-specific knowledge retrieval, web research, and contextual information. The collected evidence is analyzed and fused with the computer vision prediction to provide a more explainable and reliable diagnosis.\n\nA key feature of PlantAI is its focus on evidence-backed AI rather than simply returning a disease label. The system can provide the predicted disease, confidence information, supporting evidence, and relevant diagnostic context. When the available evidence is insufficient or the prediction is uncertain, the architecture can support uncertainty handling and abstention rather than forcing an unreliable answer.\n\nWhat makes PlantAI unique is the combination of high-performance computer vision, ensemble learning, RAG, web research, and agentic verification in a single plant-disease diagnosis workflow. This creates a multi-stage system where visual recognition is supported by external evidence and reasoning rather than operating as an isolated image classifier.\n\nThe target users can upload a plant image through the web application and receive an AI-generated diagnostic response in an accessible, conversational format. PlantAI is designed to make advanced AI-assisted plant disease analysis more accessible while providing a foundation for future agricultural decision-support applications.\n\nPlantAI demonstrates how computer vision and agentic AI can work together to transform image-based disease recognition into a more evidence-aware and reliable diagnostic workflow.\n"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"25:T403,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"PlantAI is an AI-powered plant disease diagnosis and evidence-verification system developed for the LabLab AI Hackathon.\n\nThe system uses EfficientNetV2-S for visual disease classification and an agentic verification workflow to enrich the initial prediction with disease knowledge through RAG, relevant weather/contextual information, and web research. A supervisor agent coordinates these sources and combines the available evidence to generate a more informative and explainable result.\n\nPlantAI is designed to move beyond simple image classification by incorporating evidence verification and uncertainty-aware responses. When available evidence is insufficient, the system can communicate uncertainty rather than presenting a prediction as absolute.\n\nOur EfficientNetV2-S experiments achieved 99.81% validation accuracy and 99.76% test accuracy on our experimental dataset.\n\nThe project combines deep learning, retrieval-augmented generation, agentic AI, and a practical web application into a single end-to-end workflow.\n"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"26:T4dd,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"Our team used IBM Bob for approximately 35% of the development workflow for PlantAI. IBM Bob was primarily used as an AI-assisted development tool for building and refining the frontend, integrating the frontend with our backend APIs, troubleshooting and fixing backend issues, and improving the overall application structure.\n\nSpecifically, we used IBM Bob to accelerate the implementation of the user interface and connect frontend components with the PlantAI diagnosis APIs. It also assisted us in identifying and resolving backend integration issues, debugging API communication, and improving the interaction between the computer vision inference service and the web application.\n\nIBM Bob was additionally used to help implement and refine the Docker layer of the application, including containerization and configuration needed to run the different application components consistently.\n\nOverall, IBM Bob contributed approximately 35% of our development workflow, mainly through AI-assisted frontend development, API integration, backend debugging, and Docker/containerization support. The core PlantAI AI architecture, computer vision models, ensemble approach, and disease-diagnosis methodology were developed and integrated by our team.\n"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"27:Tc34,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"Problem:\nDevelopers spend hours translating codebase realities for non-technical stakeholders. When product managers ask \"How hard is this feature?\" or clients ask \"Why is this refactor necessary?\", developers must pause their core work, inspect multiple repositories, evaluate architectural impact, and translate complex technical nuances into language suited for specific audiences (PMs, clients, managers, or support). Existing AI coding tools either write code or produce generic summaries prone to hallucinations that lack grounded architectural validation.\n\nSolution:\nI built DevLens, a developer-first codebase intelligence tool that bridges the gap between a developer’s mental model and stakeholder questions. By combining multi-repository indexing, a personalized \"Developer Lens\", and dual-engine AI validation powered by IBM Granite, DevLens delivers structured, 7-section technical impact analyses (Current System, What Would Change, Affected Areas, Effort, Risks, Unknowns, and Internal Developer Reasoning) tailored to any selected audience.\n\nTarget Users:\nSoftware engineers, tech leads, engineering managers, and technical product managers working with single repositories or multi-service microservices.\n\nHow Users Interact With It:\n1. Context \u0026 Component Indexing: Users connect GitHub repositories or multi-service projects, allowing DevLens to index file trees, dependencies, and architectural components.\n2. Define the Developer Lens: Engineers configure their investigation methodology (e.g., test-driven, data-flow first) and communication preferences (bullet points, trade-off focus), creating a reusable mental model that can be published as a public share link.\n3. Audience-Aware Analysis: Users ask any engineering question and select their audience (Developer, PM, Manager, Client, or Support). DevLens generates a structured, role-adapted breakdown.\n4. Granite Evidence Validation: IBM Granite automatically audits the analysis against indexed codebase evidence, categorizing claims (SUPPORTED, WEAKLY_SUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED) and surfacing architectural anomalies.\n5. Report Bot: Users curate multiple saved analyses into a paginated, print-ready PDF engineering report via Paprize.\n\nWhat Makes It Creative \u0026 Unique:\n- Dual-Engine Trust: Unlike single-prompt LLM wrappers, DevLens separates generation from verification. IBM Granite acts as an objective validator to ensure claims reflect actual code.\n- Developer Lens Personalization: DevLens explains systems the way you think, preserving individual engineering insights across team handoffs.\n- Multi-Audience Pitching: The exact same architectural change is automatically translated into executive summaries for management, sprint impact for PMs, or line-level reasoning for developers.\n\nEffectiveness \u0026 Efficiency:\nDevLens eliminates hours of manual drafting, cross-team misunderstandings, and unverified architectural assumptions. Running on a lightweight Cloudflare Worker with D1 SQLite persistence and non-blocking IBM Granite inference, DevLens provides instant, verified engineering intelligence with zero infrastructure overhead.\n"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"28:T81c,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"How and Where I Used IBM Bob: I utilized IBM Bob as my end-to-end AI pair-programming assistant to architect and build DevLens:\n\nDesign System \u0026 UI Engineering: I used Bob to define and implement a custom Neo-Brutalism skill (.bob/skills/neo-brutalism), establishing high-contrast design tokens, bold borders, typography, and responsive layouts across the React + Vite frontend and the Paprize PDF report generator.\nEdge Backend \u0026 D1 Schema Scaffolding: Bob helped me scaffold the serverless Cloudflare Worker backend, authoring database migration scripts (migrations/0001 to 0003) and SQLite/D1 queries for repository components, Developer Lenses, and public share links.\nAI Pipeline \u0026 Provider Architecture: Bob assisted in architecting the decoupled two-tier analysis engine in worker/src/ai/, building the evidence extraction pipeline, the validateEvidence() engine, and graceful fallback handling.\nAutomated Evaluation Suite: Bob generated the comprehensive test suite in evals/ (eval-api.js, eval-analyze.js, and eval-granite.js) to validate claim classifications, edge latency, and response schema sanitization.\nHow My Project Uses IBM Granite / watsonx.ai: DevLens integrates IBM Granite (ibm-granite/granite-3.3-8b-instruct) as a dedicated, specialized Evidence Validator Agent:\n\nZero-Hallucination Claim Verification: Once the primary model produces an engineering analysis, DevLens extracts concrete technical claims and pairs them with indexed repository code excerpts. IBM Granite acts as an impartial auditor, classifying each claim as SUPPORTED, WEAKLY_SUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED, or INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE.\nArchitectural Anomaly Detection: Granite inspects discrepancies between planned code modifications and repository context, surfacing architectural risks such as hidden component coupling, missing files, stale dependencies, and overconfident assumptions.\nResilient Edge Architecture: Granite validation runs non-fatally at the Cloudflare edge, ensuring users immediately receive their primary analysis while Granite's verification badge surfaces dynamically."])
self.__next_f.push([1,"29:T612,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"VoiceOps AI bridges conversational speech and deterministic enterprise workflows. Built with Google's Gemini 3.8 Live API and Firebase Firestore, VoiceOps AI transforms free-form spoken voice into structured, verified operational actions with sub-500ms latency.\n\nKey Capabilities:\n1. Gemini 3.8 Live Conversational Engine: Leverages real-time audio reasoning to understand complex customer requests, detect operational intent, and manage multi-turn dialogs.\n2. Low-Latency Voice Turn-Taking \u0026 Barge-in: Implements Web Audio API frequency analysis, neural voice activity detection (VAD), and instantaneous barge-in interruption so callers can change their mind mid-sentence without robotic lag.\n3. Deterministic Tool Execution \u0026 Verification: Binds natural voice commands to strict JSON schema tools (check_availability, create_booking, cancel_booking, escalate_to_human, and knowledge search). Every action is verified with reference IDs before verbal confirmation.\n4. Firebase Firestore Persistence \u0026 Auth: Provides Google Sign-In with real-time Firestore synchronization. All conversation transcripts, appointment bookings, and executed dispatch actions are securely persisted under authenticated user profiles.\n5. Real-Time Operations Pipeline: Visualizes speech input, intent detection, tool routing, dispatch execution, and verbal confirmation in an intuitive reactive dashboard.\n\nVoiceOps AI eliminates hold times, automates field scheduling, and empowers businesses to handle customer calls 24/7 with human-level naturalness and machine precision."])
self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:T51f,"])
self.__next_f.push([1,"Starting a business shouldn't require a designer, a copywriter and a week of setup. Auto Business Builder turns a spoken idea into a launch-ready business kit in minutes.\n\nHow it works: you pitch your idea by recording your voice in the browser (or uploading an audio file). AssemblyAI transcribes the speech with high accuracy, and you can review or edit the text before building. Gemini then analyses the pitch and generates a complete kit: a business name and tagline, a full landing page (hero, features, how it works, testimonials, pricing, call-to-action and a Book a Call button), three welcome emails, CRM pipeline stages, and realistic early-stage risk flags. Everything is saved and downloadable.\n\nThe standout feature is the built-in AI website editor. Open the generated landing page in a new tab and you get a Replit-style split view: a chat panel on the left and a live preview on the right. Type requests like \"change the hero to dark purple\" or \"add a pricing section\" and Gemini rewrites the page instantly, replies with a short summary of what changed, and supports one-word undo. Failed AI calls are retried silently so users never see raw errors.\n\nBuilt with Python, Flask, AssemblyAI and the Gemini API, it helps solo founders go from idea to a presentable brand and website in one sitting."])
